# The front end itself makes the object of a namespace and of an enum, in the file where they are written, and knows its layout. It wrote `anything` on the variable that holds the object, so a reader, in that
# file or in another, read every member by name off a value of which nothing was expected. The variable is expected to hold undefined or that object: by the text of the variable's own file alone.
